# Netlify redirect rules. Copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite.
# First match wins, so the SPA catch-all MUST stay last.
#
# The equivalent for Vercel lives in vercel.json at the repo root — change both.

# ── Legacy URLs (301, so link equity transfers) ───────────────────────────────
# App.tsx also has client-side <Navigate replace> for each of these. That is the
# belt; this is the braces. A client-side redirect still serves HTTP 200 for the
# old URL and only fires after the JS bundle has run, so a crawler sees a
# duplicate page rather than a moved one.
/portfolio        /work         301
/projects         /work         301
/blogs            /blog         301
/ii               /internship   301
# The programme is called Ideovent LaunchPad in 13-launchpad/, but /internship is
# the canonical URL because it is the one already linked. This alias is a 301 for
# the same reason as the four above, not a second indexable copy of the page.
# Exact match only — /blogs/<slug> is a real route and falls through to the SPA.
/launchpad        /internship   301

# ── Policy paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 03-legal-docs/policies/POLICIES-README.md publishes the documents at these
# paths; the site's routes are shorter. Both work.
/privacy-policy   /privacy      301
/refund-policy    /refund       301
# The Cookie Policy is NOT published — this site sets no analytics or advertising
# cookies and has no consent banner, so the policy would describe controls that
# do not exist. Section 13 of the Privacy Policy covers what is actually stored.
# See DEPLOY-GUIDE.md § "Legal pages".
/cookie-policy    /privacy      301

# ── SPA fallback — must be the last rule ──────────────────────────────────────
# 200, not 301: the browser keeps the requested URL and React Router renders it.
/*                /index.html   200
